# Upstream FPM tests that php-fpm-ng deliberately does not pass, one per line:
#
#   <file>.phpt   <the behaviour fpm-ng chose not to have, and the issue>
#
# The reason is mandatory. The name must be a test build/prepare.sh copied from
# sapi/fpm -- an fpmng- prefix is refused, because our own tests belong to
# build/run-fpmng-phpt.sh and are never a deviation from upstream.
#
# This is not a to-do list and not a place to park a flake. An entry says
# "upstream tests a feature we removed on purpose, so this test can only fail";
# a test that fails for any other reason is a bug to fix or an issue to open.
# The listed tests still run: the runner fails the job if one of them starts
# passing, because that means the feature came back or the entry is stale.
#
# See docs/fpm-phpt.md.

status-listen.phpt	issue #278 removed pm.status_listen and the shared status pool; a status page is now pm.status_path on the pool it describes
status-listen-expose-php-on.phpt	issue #278 removed pm.status_listen and the shared status pool; a status page is now pm.status_path on the pool it describes
status-listen-expose-php-off.phpt	issue #278 removed pm.status_listen and the shared status pool; a status page is now pm.status_path on the pool it describes
status-ping.phpt	issue #278 removed pm.status_listen and the shared status pool; ping.path stays on the pool's own listener
